codex
The earlier two defects are genuinely closed, but the final verdict is still changes requested: on Windows, target renames use `MOVEFILE_WRITE_THROUGH`, while journal creation/update still use `os.link`/`os.replace` and `_sync_directory` returns immediately. That can make target state durable while the rollback journal’s latest phase/state is not, which violates this task’s durable-recovery contract. I’m persisting that evidence and routing ordinary rework to `to-dev`.
